Why: A GTK3 window at the corner of the screen under mutter has a frame near (0,0) that differs from mutter's frame window by its invisible borders, so it was taken for Chromium's renderer-local frame and its elements came out one title bar too low; a frame that holds the client window where it really is stays a screen rectangle.

